>What exactly does the artifact, Magicbane, do?  The spoiler files that I've
>found so far don't go into much detail.

non-technical summary (SPOILERS):

Magicbane enchants pretty much like other weapons but with the added
effect that your weapon "hand" feels somehow strange afterwards.  this
is a clue that Magicbane is internally resisting (magic bane) the
enchantment.  Magicbane is an athame which, in itself, is significant.
what i've observed when wielding Magicbane follows (monsters wielding
Magicbane is another story):

Magicbane confers magic resistance and mostly (at least half the time)
just hits (doing double athame damage).  occasionally it will hit
magically with these effects:

+0 Magicbane
  never probes, mostly stuns, occasionally scares (which may be
resisted.  scaring also gets you released if you're held, swallowed,
etc.) and sometimes purges (same as cancellation.  purges on magic
users results in you gaining energy points.  purging may also be
resisted and purging sometimes appears to also scare).

+4 Magicbane
  sometimes probes (insightful probes give results like stethoscope),
sometimes stuns, sometimes scares (as above), rarely purges (as above).

+8 Magicbane
  mostly probes (as above), sometimes stuns, rarely scares (as above),
never purges.

enchantment clearly affects the way Magicbane works and each magic
attack seems to have a different potential for doing damage (purging
seems to be very damaging and probing the least damaging after normal
hits).  from these results, enchanting Magicbane seems like a barbarian
thing to do.  i've also noticed intrinsic displacement which appears to
be temporary and that occasionally monsters may get confused after a
magic attack.

in the latest release (3.1.3), Magicbane also appears to absorb curses!

Magicbane is no Vorpal Blade (etc.).  it appears to be more geared
towards combating magic attacks and magic users...

